From da4ef987756b438ad92e5ae65dd834eff32e4272 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Feb 2026 13:57:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upgrade framework to .NET 4.8, remove Simulate365 and
 ProFeatures

- Upgraded all .csproj and .vbproj projects from TargetFrameworkVersion
  v4.6.2 to v4.8 (53 project files updated)
- Removed DWSIM.Simulate365 and DWSIM.ProFeatures from the solution file
  including all build configuration entries
- Removed ProjectReference entries for both packages from DWSIM.Automation,
  DWSIM.SharedClassesCSharp, and DWSIM.vbproj
- Removed all Simulate365 import statements and replaced S365FilePickerForm
  usages with the local file picker throughout DWSIM source files:
  FormMain.vb, FormFlowsheet.vb, FormCompoundCreator.vb,
  FormDataRegression.vb, FlowsheetSurfaceControl.vb,
  SimulationObjectsPanel.vb, FormHeatMaps.vb, FormLiveFlows.vb,
  FormOptions.vb, FormSimulSettings.vb, FormSimulWizard.vb, FormWelcome.vb
- Removed all ProFeatures.Functions calls throughout the codebase; menu
  items that previously launched ProFeatures dialogs are now no-ops or
  hidden at startup
- Removed Simulate365.Services dependency from WindowsFile.cs and dropped
  the FileManagementService.FileSaved() calls
- Added GenerateFlowsheet console project under
  examples/acid-gas-removal-dynamics/ with Program.cs entry point that
  builds the acid-gas-removal dynamic flowsheet and saves it as a .dwxmz
  file using DWSIM.Automation.Automation3
